      "content": "No, ignoring these symptoms is dangerous because cat scratches often carry Cat Scratch Disease (Bartonella), an infection that frequently starts small but can progress rapidly to cause severe illness days or weeks later. Desperation is not a factor in making a medical unsafe when a spreading red line and chills appear, especially after a cat bite; medically, the cheapest in-home remedy for this is often the most expensive because it leads to hospital bills for complications. You can still find insurance support or community clinics, but please seek professional evaluation immediately rather than waiting for the line to go away",
